    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=x^2$ is the same as $y=(-x)^2$, but not $y=-x^2$. In $-x^2$, the negative sign is outside the square, so it does not get squared.",
      "worked": "$-x^2$ means $-(x^2)$: square $x$ first, then apply the negative sign. In contrast, $(-x)^2=x^2$ because the negative sign is inside the brackets.\n\nTherefore $y=-x^2$ opens downwards, whereas $y=x^2$ opens upwards.",
